From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: k230: register one gpio chip per pin

Replace the per-bank K230 GPIO driver with a per-pin driver: each
device tree node is one gpio chip with one line, whose base and id are
the global pin number, so a pin keeps the same number regardless of
which pins a board enables. gpio_chip.bgpio_lock is a raw spinlock and
the chip is identified by its fwnode.

Register accesses are serialised with the K230 hardware spinlock given
by the "hardlock" property. The wait is bounded: after
K230_HARDLOCK_TIMEOUT_US the access is skipped, an error is logged
once, and callbacks that return a status return -ETIMEDOUT.

Upstream-Status: Pending
